  "content": {
    "id": "p108-q74-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "The circle $x^2+y^2+10x-8y+16=0$ intersects the $x$-axis at $A$ and $B$, where the $x$-coordinate of $A$ is less than that of $B$, and touches the $y$-axis at $T$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p108-q74-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the coordinates of $A$, $B$ and $T$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p108-q74-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "A=(-8,0)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "B=(-2,0)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "T=(0,4)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "On the $x$-axis, $y=0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+10x+16&=0\\\\(x+8)(x+2)&=0\\\\x&=-8\\text{ or }-2\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $A$ has the smaller $x$-coordinate, $A=(-8,0)$ and $B=(-2,0)$.\n\nOn the $y$-axis, $x=0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y^2-8y+16&=0\\\\(y-4)^2&=0\\\\y&=4\\end{align*}$$\n\nHence $T=(0,4)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p108-q74-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$C$ is a point on the circle such that the line segments $BC$ and $TA$ are parallel. Find the coordinates of $C$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p108-q74-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "C=\\left(-\\frac{18}{5},-\\frac45\\right)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p108-q74-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use equal gradients to obtain ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=\\frac{x+2}{2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", then find its other intersection with the circle.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}m_{TA}&=\\frac{4-0}{0-(-8)}\\\\m_{TA}&=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $BC\\parallel TA$, the line through $B=(-2,0)$ has equation\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-0&=\\frac12(x+2)\\\\y&=\\frac{x+2}{2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt an intersection, the coordinates satisfy both the line and the circle. Substitute into the circle and multiply by $4$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)^2+10x-8\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)+16&=0\\\\4x^2+(x+2)^2+40x-16(x+2)+64&=0\\\\5x^2+28x+36&=0\\\\(x+2)(5x+18)&=0\\\\x&=-2\\text{ or }-\\frac{18}{5}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe root $x=-2$ gives $B$. For the other intersection,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{-\\frac{18}{5}+2}{2}\\\\y&=-\\frac45\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore $C=\\left(-\\frac{18}{5},-\\frac45\\right)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 118
      }
    ]
  },
